WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.520
Ever wondered what actually works when it comes to coding agents.

2
00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:08.000
Hi my name is Maria Gorinova and I'm an AI Researcher here at Tessl.

3
00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:12.280
I will be giving a webinar together with our Head of Product and Design,

4
00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:15.520
Dru Knox on the 19th of March at 4 p.m.

5
00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:16.640
UK time.

6
00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:20.760
With traditional software you can run tests, you can run static analysis.

7
00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:24.280
But when it comes to agents, things are entirely different.

8
00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:26.040
The skill that you just wrote

9
00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:29.680
might work well for one example and then completely fail the next one.

10
00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:32.840
Agents require a different way of thinking.

11
00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:36.920
In this session we will walk through designing tests for your skills

12
00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:41.120
that give you real insights What evaluation criteria should you use?

13
00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:45.040
How do you assess if your changes will work reliably?

14
00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:48.080
And how do you use some of these to continuously improve your agent's

15
00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:49.400
performance?

16
00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:54.080
If you are an engineer, a researcher or a technical leader building with agents

17
00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:57.840
and you want to make decisions grounded in data, this one is for you.

18
00:00:58.360 --> 00:00:59.600
It's free to attend.

19
00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:01.400
Follow the link to register.

20
00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:02.360
We hope to see you there.
